(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Feline chronic kidney disease commonly progresses through oxidative stress and) Tj
T*
(inflammatory mechanisms. Polyphenolic compounds have demonstrated antioxidant and anti-) Tj
T*
(inflammatory properties in experimental models. We propose a prospective trial to evaluate) Tj
T*
(whether dietary curcumin supplementation enhances renoprotection in cats with IRIS stage 3) Tj
T*
(disease. Methods: Sixteen client-owned cats with confirmed stage 3 chronic kidney disease) Tj
T*
(will be randomly assigned to receive either standard medical treatment alone \(n=8\) or) Tj
T*
(standard treatment plus daily curcumin supplementation at 80 mg divided into two doses) Tj
T*
(\(n=8\). All cats must be on stable renal diet and medication for >=2 weeks prior to) Tj
T*
(enrollment. Treatment will continue for 60 days with assessments at baseline, days 30, 45,) Tj
T*
(and 60. Primary outcome: serum creatinine-independent marker concentration \(symmetric) Tj
T*
(dimethylarginine\). Secondary outcomes: proteinuria, oxidative and inflammatory biomarkers,) Tj
T*
(and safety/tolerability. Inclusion: cats >=8 years with stable IRIS stage 3 disease and) Tj
T*
(owner compliance capacity. Study design: prospective randomized controlled trial.) Tj
